    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 58238cee253a1a0a811d30cb96804b86159ff0f4 -->\nReviewer: skull pool job review-4368, GPT-6 (Codex), mkinney; did not write or refresh this PR.\n\nClean. No blocking findings. Recommended review label: `merge-ready`.\n\nI read all 12 files in the effective diff and checked the current upstream laws. The record checks reject malformed ranges. The name lookup uses the model's facet order. Missing records and unknown picks keep their existing response shape.\n\nAll checks ran locally in `.claude/worktrees/review-4368`. The tested main base was `bc8ac92f136febef68d42bb8f413b463ebbae3d9`. The trial merge was `394a7cad812e52bb2783827d845f445b5af1e96c`; its first parent is the reviewed PR head. This base includes #4366, which supplies the followed and lost picks.\n\n**Build and tests**\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-geometry` | 457 passed |\n| app `mcp` | 66 passed |\n| app `mcp_doc_drift` | 9 passed |\n| app `mcp_pick` | 8 passed |\n| app `mcp_live` | 29 passed |\n| app `model_link` | 21 passed |\n| geometry clippy, all targets, `-D warnings` | Passed |\n| app clippy, all targets, `-D warnings` | Passed |\n| Light lane: all five test steps, release | All 11 twins passed |\n\n**Extra suites run**\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-kernel --test step_agreement`: 32 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-kernel --test machining_mesh`: 7 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test feature_edge_g1_join`: 5 passed.\n\nThe debug suites above contain 634 passing tests. They include all 17 new pinning tests. Two initial quick steps stalled on Cargo's build lock. Both passed on rerun and on the tested base.\n\n**Safety mutations**\n\nI used a temporary copy of the geometry module under `/tmp`, with the real geometry types.\n\n- Remove `record.tiles(facets)`: `a_record_that_does_not_fit_gives_no_names` failed at its assertion.\n- Suppress the unverified flag: `an_unverified_name_is_flagged` failed at its assertion.\n- The unchanged copy passed all seven tests before the mutations and after restoration.\n\n**Scope and notes**\n\nGoldens moved: none. The effective diff has no UI change or new fixture. Quick expands to batch for geometry. I ran its relevant geometry and MCP suites, plus the extra suites and all light twins. The full batch fallback, full heavy lanes, and wasm were not run.\n\nOptional, non-blocking: `crates/app/tests/mcp/source_names.rs:245` took 61.13 seconds alone and passed. A smaller named `.sc` fixture would give more time before the debug limit. I treat this as a timing note because the isolated result is close to the stated limit.\n\nThe completed checks used the cache wrapper disabled and artifacts under `target/review-local`. The worktree and branch remain for the next round. I left the labels and title unchanged.\n\nGitHub now shows this PR as ready. The author hand-off is complete. A maintainer can use this review at the feature cut.\n",
